==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|fótr}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*fōts}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*pṓds}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈfouːtʏr/}}, {{IPA|is|/ˈfouːtʰʏr/}} (Northern Iceland)
* {{audio|is|is-fótur.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|is|ouːtʏr|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# {{lb|is|anatomy}} [[foot]]
# [[leg]] (of animals and people)
# leg (of a chair, table, etc.)

====Usage notes====
* For the {{lg|proscribed}} feminine inflection, compare regional {{m|is|fjörður}}, also {{m|is|vetur}}, {{m|is|fingur}}, {{m|is|faðir}}, {{m|is|bróðir}} and to a lesser extent to nouns ending in {{m|is|-andi}} or {{m|is|-jandi}}.

